  "descriptionMarkdown": "# Bus Counter with a lil display.\nA bus counter for my singleplayer, uploading in case someone wants it. I know the circuitery could be better.<br/>\nThis is my first post, since i don't know a lot of circuitery i would love to have some advices to improve the counter.<br/>\n[Nixie Tubes Required](#https://mods.factorio.com/mod/nixie-tubes) (hiperlink to the mod)<br/>\nIn case someone wants to modify it, i'll give you the instructions on how is made aswell as some tips in case you need:<br/>\n## Modifying the blueprint for your needs:<br/>\n#### Display<br/>\nOn top we have the clock + counters.\nEach counter is composed by 5 different layers.<br/>\n[Layers](https://imgur.com/IQwwpFy)<br/>\nGray layer - Is the amount of items per minute that passes through the belt<br/>\nOrange layer - Is the amount of items in a more visual way.<br/>\nRed layer- Checks the amount of row of belts (in my case is 4, thats why I'm using 3, each 2 variables, I recommend to add another row of lamps + decider combinator in case you use more amount of belts)<br/>\nBlue layer - Checks the item amount on the belt, which is 15 for yellow, 30 for red, 45 for blue and 60 for green (EACH SIDE!)<br/>\nYellow layer - What item is checking and which colors are using the lamps.<br/>\n\nDepending on how many belt rows you'll have/need, the more lamp rows you gonna use. I recommend a minimum of 3 rows for a good amount of variables which i use at the moment:<br/>\n\nRED = 0-20% belt capacity<br/>\nRED+GREEN 20-40% belt capacity<br/>\nGREEN = 40-60% belt capacity<br/>\nGREEN + BLUE = 60-80% belt capacity<br/>\nBLUE = +80% belt capacity<br/>\n#### Logic<br/>\n##### ITEMS:\nOn the logic part we can encounter 4 more layers<br/>\n[Layers](https://imgur.com/lQNUV5t)<br/>\nGreen layer - Is a simple clock that resets each 60 ticks on R < 0, being R = -1 at the end of the clock (on R-R)<br/>\nRed layer - Is the average counter, it pushes each 60 ticks one step up (modifiable in the reset timer) <br/>\nBlue layer - Each second it pushed the items to the right to store them for the average.<br/>\nYellow layer - a part for the average counter,  divides the items / 9 to get the average and push towards the display.\n##### LIQUIDS:\nArithmetic combinator - First we transform the signal again into the requested liquid.<br/>\nArithmetic combinator - green signal minus red signal<br/>\nDecider combinator - check for negative and positive if (liquid) is < 0 or > 0<br/>\nArithmetic combinator - transform the negative into positive multiplying the liquid plus -1<br/>\nArithmetic combinator - pushes the liquids into the display.<br/>\n \n### Liquid tank differences (flow rate)<br/>\nGetting the average amount on liquids is a bit tricky, but i came to a good solution i suppose.\nInstead of checking the flow rate, we check the differece between 2 tanks, which gives us an aproximate on how much liquids we are using. If someone have a better solution, feel free to send me a msg.<br/>\n[Layers](https://imgur.com/bJ34Pie)<br/>\n\nRed layer - Just the tanks with pumps between them. (MAKE SURE YOU PUT A PUMP BETWEEN BOTH TANKS, IF YOU DON'T PUT THEM THE COUNTER WILL TELL YOU THE DIFFERENCE IS 0!!!)<br/>\nYellow layer - it goes from left to right. in this order:<br/>\nDecider combinator which takes the variable to store<br/>\nArithmetic combinator to multiply each to -1<br/>\nDecider combinator if R = 1, Everything is pushed<br/>\nArithmetic combinator to multiply each to -1 to make them possitive again (I have tried without the both -1, but i didn't make it working)<br/>\nArithmetic combinator to make the item a random var to transport the signal.<br/>\nV1<br/>\n- Initial Release<br/>\n\nV1.1<br/>\n- Increased the amount of lamps for a better colour mapping.<br/>\n- Now the average is divided by 9 to get the items throughput per second.<br/>\n- Added an average per minute.<br/>\n- Added an average of 4 on liquids.<br/>\n- Fixed the screenshots now sending to imgur directly.<br/>",
